 at least one animation\n\nSo, in the Animation tab, you'd need to create a new animation ( `Animation > New...` ). \n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3036782416/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3036869909","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108270#issuecomment-3036869909","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108270","id":3036869909,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61AvUV","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-04T16:49:42Z","updated_at":"2025-07-04T20:23:14Z","body":"I don't get a crash here with `test_crash.gdshader` on Linux with 4.5.beta 3954b2459d2dd7ae75c6a39531869a28ad8a3d5e, but it does get quite slow compared to the other shaders.\n\nHere's a HotSpot flamegraph of opening the editor with `test_crash.gdshader` assigned to the node, expanding the ShaderMaterial resource, then closing the editor:\n\n<img width=\"3745\" height=\"1307\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/855fb9fb-20a1-4c4d-b796-ad9ed4129e97\" />\n\nWith `Shader` highlighted:\n\n<img width=\"3745\" height=\"1274\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6671d29f-63a3-4e05-9499-b1ef9211e02c\" />\n\nThe slow line of code being highlighted:\n\n<img width=\"1180\" height=\"414\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8382b126-b01e-4bb7-85e4-a91b64d10ff7\" />\n\nThe RegEx cost largely dominates the cost of getting the uniform list, since a regex is used to determine what's part of a shader docs comment. I've tested moving regex creation outside the `for` loop, and it doesn't help significantly (especially since we can't move the first one outside, as it references a loop variable in its pattern). Therefore, we should look into moving away from a regex for this use case.\n\nFor reference, shader doc comments were implemented by https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/90161.\n\nProfiling data (can be opened in HotSpot): [perf.data.perfparser.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21066236/perf.data.perfparser.zip)","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3036869909/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]